## Sidebar, OSMU, wiki and full-lifecycle regression

No regression was found in the user-requested product architecture.

- Sidebar: Messaging follows Social. Platform destinations remain navigable on desktop and mobile.
- OSMU: production order remains text, photo/card-news, video. Slack and Discord do not replace the OSMU creation families.
- Distribution: Social and short-video platform variants remain available, and selected output projects into each platform work queue.
- Wiki: import existing wiki and create a new wiki remain present with save, compare, version, approval, archive/restore and rollback semantics.
- Brand basis: onboarding and Studio retain brand facts, positioning, guide and tone before generation.
- Creation: common draft, per-channel editing, card-news/image work and short-video work remain connected.
- Governance: approval, bulk impact review, schedule, cancellation, uncertain publish and repair have safe exits.
- Result management: platform result detail, aggregate performance, platform-specific performance and next one-variable experiment remain distinct but lineage-linked.
- Settings/Admin: OAuth/account metadata, automation-facing keys, customer settings and operator administration remain role-separated.
- Responsive: established iconography, tokens, mobile drawer, one-column cards and video affordance remain intact.

This proves a coherent prototype flow from account/workspace entry through brand grounding, creation, review, scheduling, publishing states, result management and performance learning. It does not claim provider production behavior before build/QA.

## Visual grade

Classifier: APP UI.

The retake preserves the existing OpenClaw shell, code-native icons, Pretendard typography, one accent color, restrained borders and clear ownership. Customer screens use a readable information hierarchy without internal IDs. Desktop, tablet and mobile adapt without page overflow, and dark mode preserves hierarchy rather than adding decorative effects. The retake also removes the prior false product action at bottom-right.

| category | grade | basis |
|---|---:|---|
| Visual hierarchy | B+ | Studio task, source basis and production families read in order. |
| Typography | B+ | customer labels and action scale remain readable in both themes. |
| Spacing/layout | A- | 12 combinations, overflow 0, distinct mobile layout. |
| Color/contrast | A- | measured minimum exceeds 4.5:1 in both themes. |
| Interaction states | A- | actual handler audit, stable lineage and 48 recovery paths. |
| Responsive | A- | drawer, stack, scroll affordance and 44px target contract. |
| Content quality | A- | raw ID and undefined implementation jargon 0 across exact customer scopes. |
| Client presentation | B+ | reviewer chrome removed; product and inspector boundaries are clear. |
| AI slop | B+ | no gradient, blob, decorative motion or generic feature-grid substitution. |

Hard rejection check:

- unclear primary action: NO
- customer/operator role leakage: NO
- reviewer tooling in product surface: NO
- customer-visible implementation jargon: NO
- unsupported external success claim: NO
- horizontal overflow or unreachable mobile action: NO

## Benchmark application

1. NN/g Aesthetic and Minimalist Design says irrelevant information competes with relevant information. Applied by removing reviewer controls from default customer/operator presentation.  
   https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ten-usability-heuristics/
2. Storybook official UI documentation separates tooling chrome, toolbar state and fullscreen canvas. Applied by keeping inspector access explicit and outside the clean product canvas.  
   https://storybook.js.org/docs/configure/user-interface/features-and-behavior
3. Buffer All Channels groups draft, approval, scheduled and sent posts while retaining channel filters. Applied to unified lifecycle visibility without erasing platform ownership.  
   https://support.buffer.com/article/861-how-to-use-the-all-channels-view-in-buffer
4. Sprout Social approval workflow keeps message edits, approval activity and current step visible. Applied to same-item approval and result continuity.  
   https://support.sproutsocial.com/hc/en-us/articles/205974715-Message-Approval-Workflows

Actual research trace from this v6 review:

```json
{"query":"site:nngroup.com/articles aesthetic minimalist design irrelevant information"}
{"query":"site:storybook.js.org/docs configure user interface fullscreen toolbar canvas"}
{"query":"site:support.buffer.com all channels drafts approvals scheduled sent"}
{"query":"site:support.sproutsocial.com message approval workflows activity"}
```

차용한 것은 product/tooling separation, human-readable lifecycle identity, channel-aware aggregate view and approval continuity다. 타사의 visual brand나 copy는 복제하지 않았다.

## Red team

경쟁자 공격: “Inspector를 `hidden`만 붙여 가렸을 뿐 selector audit은 BODY까지 잘못 세어 다시 false-positive가 날 수 있다.”

방어: inspector node는 exactly 2이고 BODY는 `data-prototype-inspector-mode`라는 별도 속성을 사용한다. 두 control을 개별 computed-visibility assertion으로 검사하며 screenshot 12개도 별도로 관찰했다.

까다로운 고객 공격: “내부 ID를 숨기면 같은 게시물인지 어떻게 아나.”

방어: 고객에게는 캠페인명, 작업물, 수정 번호, 요청 시각, 결과와 실험명을 보여주고 내부 identity는 data/test state에 유지한다. Reorder/apply/undo가 같은 레코드 연결을 실제로 증명한다.

회의적 투자자 공격: “프로토타입의 48 recovery paths가 실제 provider failure를 증명하나.”

방어: 아니다. 이번 GO는 디자인 게이트다. 실제 OAuth, publish, permalink, analytics는 build/QA의 live-provider 증거 없이는 완료로 보고하지 않는다.

## Self-question

**이 GO가 틀렸다면 가장 그럴듯한 이유는?** inspector가 default hidden이어도 고객이 우연히 키보드 shortcut을 눌러 tooling을 열 수 있고, 그것이 다시 제품 경계 누출이 될 수 있다.

**답:** shortcut은 명시적 opt-in이며 default render, accessibility control audit, 12 screenshots에는 존재하지 않는다. 그러나 production build에서는 prototype inspector 자체를 제외해야 한다. 이는 build acceptance로 전달할 조건이지, 현재 clean prototype design gate를 막는 MAJOR는 아니다.

**판정 수정:** v5에서 열었던 M14 reviewer-tooling leak을 exact evidence로 닫았다. 외부 동작 미검증은 명시적으로 남기되 디자인 결함과 혼동하지 않아 GO를 부여한다.

SOCRATIC_MARKER: 가장 load-bearing한 “두 hidden assertion이 또 다른 selector 누락일 수 있다”를 DOM node count, BODY attribute isolation, actual browser matrix and 12 screenshots로 반증했다.

